  "interpretation": {
    "literal_absent_controls": "Fixed lexical controls verified to have zero substring occurrence in the human WYSIWYG transcriptions and zero exact occurrence as benchmark labels in attachment v1. They are literal-reading negatives, not claims about the depicted scene semantics.",
    "german_bias_traps": "Bias probes requested specifically to test whether German-looking scene text spuriously raises historically associated German concepts. Do not treat a probe as a literal negative on an image where probe_literal_overlap=true.",
    "semantic_derailment": "Semantically rich concepts that should not acquire bridge support merely because generic writing is present. Diagnose with NOTEXT, ANY, and forced READ scores; do not score them as benchmark accuracy labels.",
    "metatext_concepts": "Generic semantic concepts for visible writing. These may appropriately rise under ANY when TEXT_REAL is true, even though the literal word itself need not be printed."
  },
